hadiths[12]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17115","Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu Marzuq, freedman of Tujib, and Tujib is a clan of Kindah, from Ruwayfi ibn Thabit al-Ansari, he said: I was with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he conquered Hunayn, and he stood among us addressing and said: It is not lawful for a man who believes in Allah and the Last Day to water his water to the crop of another, nor to buy booty until it is divided, nor to wear a garment from the fay of the Muslims until when he has worn it out he returns it therein, nor to ride a beast from the fay of the Muslims until when he has emaciated it he returns it therein."
"17116","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Sawadah narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Nuaym, from Wafa al-Hadrami, from Ruwayfi ibn Thabit al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever sends blessings upon Muhammad and says: O Allah, settle him in the station of nearness with You on the Day of Resurrection, my intercession becomes due for him."
"17117","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah informed us, and Qutaybah ibn Said said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Yazid, from Hanash al-Sanani, from Ruwayfi ibn Thabit, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: It is not lawful for anyone, and Qutaybah said: for a man, to water his water to the child of another, nor to fall upon a slave girl until she menstruates or her pregnancy becomes clear."
"17118","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah informed us, from al-Harith ibn Yazid, from Hanash al-Sanani, from Ruwayfi ibn Thabit, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade that a slave girl be approached until she menstruates, and pregnant women until they deliver what is in their wombs."
"17119","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us from his book, he said: Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Ayyash ibn Abbas, from Shuyaym ibn Baytan, from Abu Salim, from Shayban ibn Umayyah, from Ruwayfi ibn Thabit al-Ansari, that he raided with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: One of us would take a camel on half of what he gains, until one of us gets the arrow shaft and the other gets the head and the feathers."
"17120","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Ayyash ibn Abbas, from Shuyaym ibn Baytan, he said: Maslamah ibn Mukhallad was over the lower land. He said: He appointed Ruwayfi ibn Thabit al-Ansari, and we marched with him from Sharik to Kawm Alqam, or from Kawm Alqam to Sharik. He said: Ruwayfi ibn Thabit said: We used to raid at the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and one of us would take the camel of his brother on that he gets half of what he gains. He said: Until one of us gets the arrow shaft and the other gets the head and the feathers. He said: Ruwayfi ibn Thabit said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: O Ruwayfi, life will perhaps be long for you, so inform the people that whoever knots his beard, or wears a string amulet, or cleans himself with the dung of a beast or a bone, has disavowed what Allah sent down upon Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"17121","Hasan ibn Musa al-Ashyab narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah informed us, he said: Ayyash ibn Abbas narrated to us, from Shuyaym ibn Baytan, he said: Ruwayfi ibn Thabit narrated to us, he said: One of us in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would take the camel of his brother on that he give him half of what he gains, and he gets half, until one of us gets the head and the feathers and the other gets the shaft. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: O Ruwayfi, life will perhaps be long for you, so inform the people that whoever knots his beard, or wears a string amulet, or cleans himself with the dung of a beast or a bone, then Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, is free of him."
"17122","Yaqub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Abu Marzuq, freedman of Tujib, from Hanash al-Sanani, he said: We raided with Ruwayfi ibn Thabit al-Ansari a village of the villages of the Maghreb called Jarabbah. He stood among us addressing and said: O people, I say among you only what I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say. He stood among us on the day of Hunayn and said: It is not lawful for a man who believes in Allah and the Last Day to water his water to the crop of another, meaning approaching pregnant women among the captives, and to touch a previously married woman among the captives until he clears her womb, meaning when he buys her, and to sell booty until it is divided, and to ride a beast from the fay of the Muslims until when he has emaciated it he returns it therein, and to wear a garment from the fay of the Muslims until when he has worn it out he returns it therein."
"17123","Yaqub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq: Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Jafar al-Misri narrated to me, he said: One who heard Hanash al-Sanani narrated to me, he says: I heard Ruwayfi ibn Thabit al-Ansari say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not buy gold for gold except weight for weight, nor marry a previously married woman among the captives until she menstruates."
"17124","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Yazid, he said: Hanash narrated to me, he said: We were with Ruwayfi ibn Thabit in the expedition of Jarabbah, and he divided it among us, and Ruwayfi said to us: Whoever gets any of these captives, let him not tread her until she menstruates, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: It is not lawful for a man to water his water to the child of another."
"17125","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, he said: al-Mufaddal narrated to us, he said: Ayyash ibn Abbas narrated to me that Shuyaym ibn Baytan informed him that he heard Shayban al-Qitbani say: Maslamah ibn Mukhallad left Ruwayfi ibn Thabit al-Ansari in charge over the lower land. He said: We marched with him. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: O Ruwayfi, life will perhaps be long for you after me, so inform the people that whoever knots his beard, or wears a string amulet, or cleans himself with the dung of a beast or with a bone, then Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, is free of him."
"17126","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, he said: Maslamah ibn Mukhallad, and he was commander over Egypt, offered Ruwayfi ibn Thabit to appoint him over the tithes. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The owner of the maks is in the Fire."
